        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "95af31ba-04bc-5a9d-a898-8191166060aa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Oera Linda Book\n- Languages: Old Frisian\n- People: Friso, Martinus Hamconius, Alexander the Great\n- Places: Punjab, Rhine, Weser, European North Sea coast\n- Topics: Frisian colonists, historical mythology, religious themes\n\nFacts:\n- The Oera Linda Book is a manuscript written in a form of Old Frisian.\n- The Oera Linda Book purports to cover historical, mythological, and religious themes from 2194 BCE to 803 CE.\n- Old Frisian is a West Germanic language spoken between the 8th and 16th centuries.\n- Old Frisian was spoken in the area between the Rhine and Weser on the European North Sea coast.\n- Martinus Hamconius wrote the 17th century chronicle \"Frisia seu de viris rebusque illustribus\".\n- According to Martinus Hamconius and the 19th century Oera Linda Book, Friso was a leader of Frisian colonists in the Punjab.\n- According to Martinus Hamconius and the Oera Linda Book, Friso's group had been settled in the Punjab for well over a millennium when Alexander the Great discovered them.",
